echo -e 'hello how are you??' | grep 'hello' --color=always

grep -v is used to print all the line's expect the pattern matched file.

echo -e "1 2 3 4\nhello\n5 6" | egrep -c "[0-9]"

or 

echo -e "1 2 3 4\nhello\n5 6" | grep -E -c "[0-9]"

grep "text" . -r -n where -R and -r is used for recursively searching of the folder.

echo "hello world" | grep -i "HELLO" where -i is used to ignore the case.

Matching mulitple patterns
--------------------------

echo "this is a line of text" | grep  -e "this" -e "line" -o  

grep "main()" . -r --include *.{c,cpp}

the above command is used to find only in this c and cpp file's

--exclude is used exclude that particular file or file's


